Subject: [PATCH 11/20] B3-1 (H-1): session-manager admission-before-spawn
 (two-phase verdict)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

spawn() now asks the supervisor for a verdict BEFORE the PTY factory runs: a pre-spawn refusal means no OS process ever starts (no registry record, no killable thing — the refusal is total, and the id stays immediately reusable). The post-spawn admit is retained as the pid-binding verdict and re-verifies the channel that may have dropped between the two calls; that path keeps the existing fail-closed REFUSED + kill semantics byte-for-byte. A throwing supervisor is denial at the pre-spawn verdict too. View sinks still receive a refused event (preSpawn: true, pid: null).

Tests: the two denial tests were rewritten for the new contract and three regression tests added — verdict ORDER (admit:pre, spawn, admit:post), post-spawn verdict carries the real pid, channel-drop-between-verdicts kills and marks REFUSED. Fail-before (original file byte-restored via git show): 18/23, the 5 H-1 tests fail with the factory having spawned despite refusal (1 !== 0). Pass-after: 23/23.

U186 falsification pin: main.js changed by ONE comment-only edit (H-1 closure note on RENDERER_SPEC_ALLOWED_KEYS). All 37 pane_input_bypass mutations re-read against the new bytes, harness re-run: ALL MUTATIONS CAUGHT, main.js restored BYTE-IDENTICAL (E334706C…); zero CR bytes verified (U274). Full desktop suite 1104/1104 OK.

